# Connection string pooled de Supabase (Supavisor, puerto 6543).
# Copiar este archivo a .env y completar con la URL real (Session pooler).
SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres


1. Install (once):
py -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\python -m pip install -e "packages/shared[dev]" -e "services/etl[dev]" -e "services/api[dev]"
2. Set .env: create .env at repo root with SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres (pooled string, port 6543).
3. Load DB (once, from repo root):
.venv\Scripts\python -m shared.migrate
.venv\Scripts\python -m etl.main
4. Terminal 1 — API:
.venv\Scripts\python -m api.app
5. Terminal 2 — dashboard:
.venv\Scripts\python -m http.server 8080 --directory frontend
6. Open http://127.0.0.1:8080/.